01C2   D1                     POP   DE   
01C3   2B                     DEC   HL   
01C4   72                     LD   (HL),D   
01C5   2B                     DEC   HL   
01C6   73                     LD   (HL),E   
01C7   05                     DEC   B   
01C8   D9                     EXX      
01C9   CC 2E 04               CALL   Z,pollk   
01CC   F7                     RST   30h   
01CD                             ; ---- machine code: the grave -----------------------------------------------
01CD                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
01CD                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (C9h) is
01CD                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
01CD                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
01CD                             ; code is entered by CALL with the data stack above the return address; it
01CD                             ; must keep BC, and on return the top cell becomes the new TOS.
01CD   CD E2 03     H_GRAVE:   CALL   hexc   
01D0   30 CA                  JR   NC,exec   
01D2   77           HX1:      LD   (HL),A   ; the high digit goes in first ...
01D3   CD E2 03               CALL   hexc   
01D6   30 08                  JR   NC,hx2   ; odd digit: consumed, and the RET below
01D8   ED 6F                  RLD      ;   overwrites it
01DA   23                     INC   HL   ; ... and RLD shifts it up under the low one
01DB   CD E2 03               CALL   hexc   
01DE   38 F2                  JR   C,hx1   
01E0   36 C9        HX2:      LD   (HL),0C9h   ; (never range-checked: the spec says so)
01E2   F7                     RST   30h   
01E3                             ; ---- where the two pages meet ----------------------------------------------
01E3                             ; The first page ends somewhere among the next four handlers, ] \ [ @ (they
01E3                             ; are in falling code order for this), and where exactly differs between the
01E3                             ; builds: NPG1 follows. Every handler below these four must start in the
01E3                             ; second page, and every one above in the first; chktab.py checks both.
01E3                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it.
